Description: export the replicant factory symbols from the executable
 The Deskbar resolves this tray item by loading the provider image named
 in the archive's "add_on" string and looking up instantiate_deskbar_item
 and USBDeskbarView::Instantiate(BMessage*). A plain executable keeps
 those symbols in .symtab only, which the loader cannot see, so the
 replicant would come back grey. Link with -rdynamic so the factory
 symbols reach the dynamic symbol table - the same export contract the
 tree's own replicant apps get from the runnable-add-on link rule, which
 the Makefile-Engine does not implement.
Author: Dario Casalinuovo <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
 COMPILER_FLAGS =
 
 #	specify additional linker flags
-LINKER_FLAGS =
+LINKER_FLAGS = -rdynamic
 
 #	specify the version of this particular item
 APP_VERSION = 1 0 0
